  "id": "guanfacine",
  "term": "guanfacine",
  "definition": "Guanfacine is a non-stimulant medication that acts on alpha-2 adrenergic receptors and is used in children with ADHD to reduce symptoms. It has mild sedating effects and may be especially helpful for behavioral symptoms such as hyperactivity, but it is also associated with relatively poor tolerability because side effects often lead people to stop taking it.",
